import EGF.SphereFamilies
import Mathlib.Dynamics.Ergodic.Action.OfMinimal
import Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Projection.FiniteDimensional

/-!
# Theorem 3.6 from density: rotations generating a dense subgroup of `SO(n)`, `n ≥ 2`, act ergodically on `S^{n−1}`, so a rich isometry spherical family is universal

`theo:universality_sphere` — `main.tex:305` (Section 3.1.3, `main.tex:295–310`; Appendix B.3,
`main.tex:826–837`). Not marked: Theorem 3.6 holds only with C-31's richness (its printed form is
refuted, here also on `𝕊²`), see SCOPE. Anchors the density form of C-28 (sphere half) and C-49
for every `d ≥ 1`, and the last clause of C-32's corrected text.

> An isometry spherical family is a universal EGF family, provided technical assumptions on the
> $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$. (`main.tex:305`)

> The technical assumption is satisfied if the $\Phi_i$ have algebraic coefficients and are frozen:
> this is a consequence of the main theorem of \citet{bourgain2012spectral} (see also
> \citet{benoist2016spectral}) that guarantees a spectral gap under this assumption. Furthermore,
> the main Theorem of \citet{breuillard2003dense} allows to build a dense subgroup of
> $\mathrm{SO}_{d}(\mathbb R)$ with two generators and algebraic coefficients. Therefore, EGF are
> universal on spheres with $p=4$ and well-chosen $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^4$: the two generators and
> their inverse. (`main.tex:307–308`)

> With the technical condition "The set of transforms $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ is stable by inverse, the
> group generated by $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ is dense in $\mathrm{SO}(d,\mathbb R)$ and each of the
> $\Phi_i$ has algebraic coefficients", Theorem \ref{theo:universality_sphere} then follows from
> master Theorem \ref{theo:universality_true}. (`main.tex:836`)

## What is proved

| | |
|---|---|
| `instIsTopologicalGroupSO`, `instCompactSpaceSO`, `instSecondCountableTopologySO`, `instMeasurableSpaceSO`, `soHaar`, `instIsMulRightInvariantSoHaar` | `SO(n)` a compact second-countable group, named instances; its Haar probability, left and right invariant |
| `instMulActionSOSphere`, `instContinuousSMulSOSphere`, `instSMulInvariantMeasureSOSphere` | `SO(n)` acts continuously on `S^{n−1}` preserving `σ` |
| `exists_rotSphere_eq`, `not_transitive_rotSphere_one` | transitive for `n ≥ 2` (two reflections); not for `n = 1` |
| `sphereVolume_eq_smul_map_orbit`, `ergodicSMul_rotSphere` | `σ = σ(S) · (A ↦ Ax₀)₊ Haar` (Fubini); `SO(n)` is ergodic on `(S^{n−1}, σ)`, `n ≥ 2` |
| `ae_const_of_dense_rotations`, `isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_of_dense` | **density ⇒ ergodicity**: Mathlib's `aeconst_of_dense_aestabilizer_smul` |
| `universality_sphere`, `universality_sphere_of_printedCondition`, `universality_sphere_l2` | **Theorem 3.6 corrected** (C-28, C-31, C-49), every `𝕊^d`, `d ≥ 1` |
| `UniversalitySphereDense`, `universalitySphereDense_iff` | the density form holds on `𝕊^d` iff `d ≥ 1` (`S⁰` refutes it) |
| `so3_euler`, `so3Witness`, `so3Witness_dense`, `universality_sphere_witness_three` | Euler angles; two rational rotations of `SO(3)` and their inverses, dense (`p = 4`, `main.tex:308` on `𝕊²`) |
| `not_universalitySpherePrinted_two` | **C-31** on `𝕊²`: the printed Theorem 3.6 fails at `so3Witness` |

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis (`main.tex:305`, `:307`, `:836`) | here (`universality_sphere`) |
|---|---|
| `Φᵢ ∈ SO_{d+1}(ℝ)` acting on `𝕊^d` | ✓ carried: `Φ : Fin p → SO n`, `n = d + 1`, `x ↦ Ax` |
| `𝕊^d` a sphere of positive dimension (a reading: the paper does not exclude `d = 0`) | ⚠ added: `2 ≤ n`, i.e. `d ≥ 1`; needed (`not_universalitySphereDense_zero`) |
| the generated group dense in `SO(d, ℝ)` (`:836`) | ✓ carried: `Dense (Subgroup.closure (range Φ))` in `SO n` |
| stable under inverse (`:836`) | ⚠ weakened: dropped |
| algebraic coefficients (`:307`, `:836`) | ⚠ weakened: dropped |
| frozen (`:307`) | ✓ the rich model contains the uniform kernel of the given `Φ` |
| spectral gap (Bourgain–Gamburd, `:307`) | ⚠ weakened: dropped |
| an isometry spherical family (`:303`) | ⚠ weakened: any family `𝓕` |
| (unstated) the model realizes `αⁱ ≡ 1/p` and outflows dense in the non-negative cone of `L²(σ)` | ⚠ strengthened: `IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕` (C-31), needed (`not_isUniversalFamilyEps_sphere_of_constantHeads`) |
| "universal EGF family" | the ε-form of record `IsUniversalFamilyEps σ 𝓕` (DEC-141) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

Readings (as `EGF/SphereFamilies.lean`): `σ = volume.toSphere`; `SO(n)` is
`Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ` with the subspace topology and the Borel σ-algebra
(named instances: a future Mathlib instance on matrices would be a second path); `𝕊^d` is
`RoundSphere (d + 1)`; "dense in `SO(d, ℝ)`" is read in the group the rotations live in,
`SO(d + 1)` (C-32's index slip); "the group generated" is the subgroup. `𝕊^d` is read with
`d ≥ 1`: on `S⁰` the density form fails (`SO(1)` is trivial). Non-vacuity: dense families are
given for `n = 2` (`so2Witness`) and `n = 3` (`so3Witness`); for `n ≥ 4` none is given (the
paper cites `breuillard2003dense` for one; an induction through the stabilizer of `eₙ` is not
formalized), so there `universality_sphere` is proved but not instantiated. Not proved: density
of the six `π/4` rotations of `main.tex:496`; that density is necessary (it is not in general).

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
-/

namespace EGF

open MeasureTheory Filter Set
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology Pointwise Matrix

/-! ## `SO(n)`: a compact, second-countable topological group with its Haar probability -/

/-- `SO(n)` is a topological group: multiplication is continuous and the inverse is `A ↦ Aᵀ`. -/
instance instIsTopologicalGroupSO (n : ℕ) : IsTopologicalGroup (SO n) where
  toContinuousMul := Submonoid.continuousMul _
  continuous_inv := by
    have h : (fun A : SO n => ((A⁻¹ : SO n) : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)) =
        fun A : SO n => star (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) := rfl
    refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
    rw [Function.comp_def, h]
    exact continuous_star.comp continuous_subtype_val

/-- `SO(n)` is closed in the matrices. -/
theorem isClosed_specialOrthogonalGroup (n : ℕ) :
    IsClosed (Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ : Set (Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)) := by
  have h : (Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ : Set (Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)) =
      {A | A * star A = 1} ∩ {A | A.det = 1} := by
    ext A
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_orthogonalGroup_iff,
      Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_setOf_eq]
    rfl
  rw [h]
  exact (isClosed_eq (continuous_id.mul continuous_star) continuous_const).inter
    (isClosed_eq (Continuous.matrix_det continuous_id) continuous_const)

/-- `SO(n)` is compact. -/
instance instCompactSpaceSO (n : ℕ) : CompactSpace (SO n) := by
  refine isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp ?_
  have hsub : (Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin n) ℝ : Set (Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)) ⊆
      Set.pi univ fun _ => Set.pi univ fun _ => Metric.closedBall (0 : ℝ) 1 := by
    intro A hA i _ j _
    rw [Metric.mem_closedBall, dist_zero_right]
    exact entry_norm_bound_of_unitary (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.1 hA).1 i j
  exact (isCompact_univ_pi fun _ => isCompact_univ_pi fun _ => isCompact_closedBall _ _).of_isClosed_subset
    (isClosed_specialOrthogonalGroup n) hsub

/-- `SO(n)` is second countable (a subspace of `ℝ^{n×n}`). -/
instance instSecondCountableTopologySO (n : ℕ) : SecondCountableTopology (SO n) := by
  haveI : SecondCountableTopology (Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) :=
    inferInstanceAs (SecondCountableTopology (Fin n → Fin n → ℝ))
  exact TopologicalSpace.Subtype.secondCountableTopology _

/-- The Borel σ-algebra of `SO(n)`. -/
noncomputable instance instMeasurableSpaceSO (n : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace (SO n) := borel _

instance instBorelSpaceSO (n : ℕ) : BorelSpace (SO n) := ⟨rfl⟩

/-- **The Haar probability of `SO(n)`** (`haarMeasure ⊤`, normalized on the whole compact group). -/
noncomputable def soHaar (n : ℕ) : Measure (SO n) := Measure.haarMeasure ⊤

instance instIsHaarMeasureSoHaar (n : ℕ) : (soHaar n).IsHaarMeasure :=
  Measure.isHaarMeasure_haarMeasure _

instance instIsProbabilityMeasureSoHaar (n : ℕ) : IsProbabilityMeasure (soHaar n) := ⟨by
  have h := Measure.haarMeasure_self (K₀ := (⊤ : TopologicalSpace.PositiveCompacts (SO n)))
  simpa [soHaar] using h⟩

/-- **A compact group is unimodular**: `soHaar n` is also right invariant. -/
instance instIsMulRightInvariantSoHaar (n : ℕ) : (soHaar n).IsMulRightInvariant := ⟨fun g => by
  have h := Measure.isMulInvariant_eq_smul_of_compactSpace ((soHaar n).map (· * g)) (soHaar n)
  have h1 : ((soHaar n).map (· * g)) univ = 1 := by
    rw [Measure.map_apply (measurable_mul_const g) MeasurableSet.univ, Set.preimage_univ,
      measure_univ]
  have hc : Measure.haarScalarFactor ((soHaar n).map (· * g)) (soHaar n) = 1 := by
    have h2 := congrArg (fun μ : Measure (SO n) => μ univ) h
    rw [Measure.smul_apply, h1, measure_univ, ENNReal.smul_def, smul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h2
    exact_mod_cast h2.symm
  rw [h, hc, one_smul]⟩

/-! ## `SO(n)` acting on the sphere -/

/-- **`SO(n)` acts on `S^{n−1}`** by `A • x = Ax` (`rotSphere`). -/
noncomputable instance instMulActionSOSphere (n : ℕ) : MulAction (SO n) (RoundSphere n) where
  smul A x := rotSphere A x
  one_smul := rotSphere_one
  mul_smul A B x := rotSphere_mul A B x

theorem smul_eq_rotSphere {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) (x : RoundSphere n) : A • x = rotSphere A x := rfl

/-- The action is jointly continuous. -/
instance instContinuousSMulSOSphere (n : ℕ) : ContinuousSMul (SO n) (RoundSphere n) := by
  refine ⟨Continuous.subtype_mk ?_ _⟩
  have h : (fun p : SO n × RoundSphere n => rotLIE p.1 (p.2 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) =
      fun p => WithLp.toLp 2
        ((p.1 : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) *ᵥ WithLp.ofLp (p.2 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) := by
    funext p
    rw [← ofLp_rotLIE]
  show Continuous (fun p : SO n × RoundSphere n => rotLIE p.1 (p.2 : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
  rw [h]
  refine (PiLp.continuous_toLp 2 _).comp ?_
  exact (continuous_subtype_val.comp continuous_fst).matrix_mulVec
    ((PiLp.continuous_ofLp 2 _).comp (continuous_subtype_val.comp continuous_snd))

/-- Rotations preserve `σ`. -/
instance instSMulInvariantMeasureSOSphere (n : ℕ) :
    SMulInvariantMeasure (SO n) (RoundSphere n) (sphereVolume n) :=
  ⟨fun A _ hs => (measurePreserving_rotSphere A).measure_preimage hs.nullMeasurableSet⟩

/-! ## Transitivity on the sphere for `n ≥ 2` -/

/-- A linear isometry of `ℝⁿ` of determinant `1` is a rotation `x ↦ Ax`, `A ∈ SO(n)`. -/
theorem exists_SO_of_det_eq_one {n : ℕ}
    (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (hf : LinearMap.det (f.toLinearEquiv : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →ₗ[ℝ] _) = 1) :
    ∃ A : SO n, ∀ v, rotLIE A v = f v := by
  classical
  set b := EuclideanSpace.basisFun (Fin n) ℝ
  set M := LinearMap.toMatrix b.toBasis b.toBasis
    (f.toLinearEquiv : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →ₗ[ℝ] _) with hMdef
  have hM : M ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin n) ℝ := f.toMatrix_mem_unitaryGroup b b
  have hdet : M.det = 1 := by rw [hMdef, LinearMap.det_toMatrix]; exact hf
  refine ⟨⟨M, Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.2 ⟨hM, hdet⟩⟩, fun v => ?_⟩
  apply WithLp.ofLp_injective 2
  rw [ofLp_rotLIE]
  have hmv := LinearMap.toMatrix_mulVec_repr b.toBasis b.toBasis
    (f.toLinearEquiv : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →ₗ[ℝ] _) v
  have hrepr : ∀ w : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n), ⇑(b.toBasis.repr w) = WithLp.ofLp w := fun w =>
    funext fun j => by rw [OrthonormalBasis.coe_toBasis_repr_apply, EuclideanSpace.basisFun_repr]
  rw [hrepr, hrepr] at hmv
  exact hmv

/-- **`SO(n)` is transitive on `S^{n−1}` for `n ≥ 2`**: the reflection in `(x − y)⊥`, composed
with a reflection fixing `y`. -/
theorem exists_rotSphere_eq {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (x y : RoundSphere n) :
    ∃ A : SO n, rotSphere A x = y := by
  by_cases hxy : x = y
  · exact ⟨1, by rw [hxy, rotSphere_one]⟩
  have hxy' : (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) - y ≠ 0 :=
    sub_ne_zero.2 fun h => hxy (Subtype.ext h)
  -- a non-zero vector orthogonal to `y`
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hv0⟩ : ∃ v ∈ (ℝ ∙ (y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))ᗮ, v ≠ 0 := by
    apply Submodule.exists_mem_ne_zero_of_ne_bot
    intro hbot
    have h1 := Submodule.finrank_add_finrank_orthogonal (ℝ ∙ (y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    rw [hbot, finrank_bot, add_zero, finrank_euclideanSpace_fin] at h1
    have h2 := finrank_span_le_card (R := ℝ) ({(y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} : Set _)
    rw [Set.toFinset_singleton, Finset.card_singleton] at h2
    omega
  set R₁ := Submodule.reflection (ℝ ∙ ((x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) - y))ᗮ with hR₁
  set R₂ := Submodule.reflection (ℝ ∙ v)ᗮ with hR₂
  have h1 : R₁ x = y := Submodule.reflection_sub (by simp)
  have h2 : R₂ y = y := by
    refine Submodule.reflection_mem_subspace_eq_self ?_
    rw [Submodule.mem_orthogonal_singleton_iff_inner_right]
    rw [Submodule.mem_orthogonal_singleton_iff_inner_right] at hv
    rw [real_inner_comm]
    exact hv
  have hdet : ∀ w : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n), w ≠ 0 →
      LinearMap.det (Submodule.reflection (ℝ ∙ w)ᗮ).toLinearMap = -1 := fun w hw => by
    rw [Submodule.det_reflection, Submodule.orthogonal_orthogonal, finrank_span_singleton hw,
      pow_one]
  obtain ⟨A, hA⟩ := exists_SO_of_det_eq_one (R₁.trans R₂) (by
    show LinearMap.det (R₂.toLinearMap ∘ₗ R₁.toLinearMap) = 1
    rw [LinearMap.det_comp, hR₁, hR₂, hdet _ hv0, hdet _ hxy']
    norm_num)
  refine ⟨A, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  show rotLIE A x = y
  rw [hA, LinearIsometryEquiv.trans_apply, h1, h2]

/-- **`SO(1)` is trivial**: a `1 × 1` matrix of determinant `1` is `1`. -/
theorem eq_one_of_SO_one (A : SO 1) : A = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  have hdet := (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.1 A.2).2
  rw [Matrix.det_unique] at hdet
  ext i j
  rw [Subsingleton.elim i default, Subsingleton.elim j default]
  exact hdet

/-- **For `n = 1` transitivity fails**: `SO(1)` is trivial and `S⁰` has two points. -/
theorem not_transitive_rotSphere_one : ¬ ∀ x y : RoundSphere 1, ∃ A : SO 1, rotSphere A x = y := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨A, hA⟩ := h ⟨EuclideanSpace.single 0 1, by simp⟩ ⟨EuclideanSpace.single 0 (-1), by simp⟩
  rw [eq_one_of_SO_one A, rotSphere_one] at hA
  have h0 := congrArg (fun z : RoundSphere 1 => (z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 1)) 0) hA
  simp only [PiLp.single_apply, if_true] at h0
  norm_num at h0

/-! ## Ergodicity of `SO(n)` on the sphere, and of its dense subgroups -/

/-- **`σ` is a multiple of an orbit pushforward of Haar** (Fubini on `SO(n) × S^{n−1}`, with
transitivity and right invariance). -/
theorem sphereVolume_eq_smul_map_orbit {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (x₀ : RoundSphere n) :
    sphereVolume n = sphereVolume n univ • (soHaar n).map (fun A => rotSphere A x₀) := by
  have hmeas : Measurable (fun A : SO n => rotSphere A x₀) :=
    (continuous_id.smul (continuous_const (y := x₀))).measurable
  ext s hs
  rw [Measure.smul_apply, Measure.map_apply hmeas hs, smul_eq_mul]
  set E : Set (SO n × RoundSphere n) := {p | p.1 • p.2 ∈ s} with hEdef
  have hE : MeasurableSet E := continuous_smul.measurable hs
  have hfst := Measure.prod_apply (μ := soHaar n) (ν := sphereVolume n) hE
  have hsnd := Measure.prod_apply_symm (μ := soHaar n) (ν := sphereVolume n) hE
  have h1 : ∀ A : SO n, sphereVolume n (Prod.mk A ⁻¹' E) = sphereVolume n s := fun A =>
    (measurePreserving_rotSphere A).measure_preimage hs.nullMeasurableSet
  have h2 : ∀ x : RoundSphere n, soHaar n ((fun A => (A, x)) ⁻¹' E) =
      soHaar n ((fun A => rotSphere A x₀) ⁻¹' s) := fun x => by
    obtain ⟨h, rfl⟩ := exists_rotSphere_eq hn x₀ x
    have hset : (fun A => (A, rotSphere h x₀)) ⁻¹' E =
        (fun A => A * h) ⁻¹' ((fun A => rotSphere A x₀) ⁻¹' s) := by
      ext A
      simp only [hEdef, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_setOf_eq, smul_eq_rotSphere, rotSphere_mul]
    rw [hset, measure_preimage_mul_right]
  simp_rw [h1] at hfst
  simp_rw [h2] at hsnd
  rw [lintegral_const, measure_univ, mul_one] at hfst
  rw [lintegral_const] at hsnd
  rw [← hfst, hsnd, mul_comm]

/-- **`SO(n)` acts ergodically on `(S^{n−1}, σ)` for `n ≥ 2`.** -/
theorem ergodicSMul_rotSphere {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) :
    ErgodicSMul (SO n) (RoundSphere n) (sphereVolume n) := by
  obtain ⟨x₀⟩ : Nonempty (RoundSphere n) := ⟨⟨EuclideanSpace.single ⟨0, by omega⟩ 1, by simp⟩⟩
  set o : SO n → RoundSphere n := fun A => rotSphere A x₀ with ho
  have hmeas : Measurable o := (continuous_id.smul (continuous_const (y := x₀))).measurable
  have hσ := sphereVolume_eq_smul_map_orbit hn x₀
  have hpos : sphereVolume n univ ≠ 0 := sphereVolume_univ_ne_zero (by omega)
  have hkey : ∀ s, MeasurableSet s →
      sphereVolume n s = sphereVolume n univ * soHaar n (o ⁻¹' s) := fun s hs => by
    conv_lhs => rw [hσ]
    rw [Measure.smul_apply, Measure.map_apply hmeas hs, smul_eq_mul]
  have hqmp : Measure.QuasiMeasurePreserving o (soHaar n) (sphereVolume n) := by
    refine ⟨hmeas, Measure.AbsolutelyContinuous.mk fun s hs h0 => ?_⟩
    rw [Measure.map_apply hmeas hs]
    have h := hkey s hs
    rw [h0, eq_comm, mul_eq_zero] at h
    exact h.resolve_left hpos
  refine { toSMulInvariantMeasure := inferInstance,
           aeconst_of_forall_preimage_smul_ae_eq := fun {s} hs hinv => ?_ }
  have hB : ∀ g : SO n, (fun A => g • A) ⁻¹' (o ⁻¹' s) =ᵐ[soHaar n] o ⁻¹' s := fun g => by
    have hset : (fun A => g • A) ⁻¹' (o ⁻¹' s) = o ⁻¹' ((fun x => g • x) ⁻¹' s) := by
      ext A
      simp only [ho, Set.mem_preimage, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_rotSphere, rotSphere_mul]
    rw [hset]
    exact hqmp.preimage_ae_eq (hinv g)
  have hc := aeconst_of_forall_preimage_smul_ae_eq (SO n) (hmeas hs).nullMeasurableSet hB
  rcases eventuallyConst_set'.1 hc with h0 | h1
  · refine eventuallyConst_set'.2 (Or.inl (ae_eq_empty.2 ?_))
    rw [hkey s hs, ae_eq_empty.1 h0, mul_zero]
  · refine eventuallyConst_set'.2 (Or.inr (ae_eq_univ.2 ?_))
    rw [hkey sᶜ hs.compl, Set.preimage_compl, ae_eq_univ.1 h1, mul_zero]

/-- **Rotations generating a dense subgroup of `SO(n)`, `n ≥ 2`, have no non-trivial common
a.e.-invariant set.** -/
theorem ae_const_of_dense_rotations {n p : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n))) :
    ∀ A, MeasurableSet A → (∀ i, rotSphere (Φ i) ⁻¹' A =ᵐ[sphereVolume n] A) →
      sphereVolume n A = 0 ∨ sphereVolume n Aᶜ = 0 := by
  intro A hA hinv
  haveI := ergodicSMul_rotSphere hn
  have hsub : Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) ≤
      MulAction.aestabilizer (SO n) (sphereVolume n) A := by
    rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    have h : (Φ i)⁻¹ ∈ MulAction.aestabilizer (SO n) (sphereVolume n) A := by
      rw [MulAction.mem_aestabilizer, ← Set.preimage_smul]
      exact hinv i
    simpa using inv_mem h
  have hd : Dense (MulAction.aestabilizer (SO n) (sphereVolume n) A : Set (SO n)) :=
    hdense.mono (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.2 hsub)
  have hc := aeconst_of_dense_aestabilizer_smul hA.nullMeasurableSet hd
  rcases eventuallyConst_set'.1 hc with h0 | h1
  · exact Or.inl (ae_eq_empty.1 h0)
  · exact Or.inr (ae_eq_univ.1 h1)

/-- The generated group of permutations acts ergodically. -/
theorem isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_of_dense {n p : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n))) :
    IsGroupErgodic (sphereVolume n) (sphereRotGroup Φ) :=
  (isGroupErgodic_sphereRotGroup_iff Φ).2 (ae_const_of_dense_rotations hn Φ hdense)

/-! ## Theorem 3.6 -/

/-- **Theorem 3.6, corrected** (C-28, C-31, C-49). -/
theorem universality_sphere {n p : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n)))
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n))) (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) 𝓕 :=
  universality_sphere_of_ergodic (by omega) Φ (ae_const_of_dense_rotations hn Φ hdense) 𝓕 hrich

/-- **The printed technical assumption, completed by C-31's richness, suffices on every `𝕊^d`,
`d ≥ 1`**: of the condition of `main.tex:836` (stable under inverse, dense, algebraic entries) only
the density clause is used. -/
theorem universality_sphere_of_printedCondition {n p : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (hΦ : IsPrintedSphereCondition Φ) (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere n)))
    (hrich : IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕) : IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) 𝓕 :=
  universality_sphere hn Φ hΦ.2.1 𝓕 hrich

/-- **Theorem 3.6 for the `L²` model**: rotations generating a dense subgroup of `SO(n)`, `n ≥ 2`,
make the family of the `L²` model (uniform softmax head, every non-negative `L²` outflow)
ε-universal. -/
theorem universality_sphere_l2 {n p : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (hp : 0 < p) (Φ : Fin p → SO n)
    (hdense : Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO n)) : Set (SO n))) :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume n) (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel hp Φ)) :=
  universality_sphere hn Φ hdense _ (isRichSphericalModel_l2 hp Φ)

/-- **The density form of Theorem 3.6 on `𝕊^d`** (C-28's corrected Theorem 3.6, C-49's l.307):
for every finite family of rotations `Φᵢ ∈ SO(d + 1)` generating a dense subgroup, every family
`𝓕` rich at the `Φᵢ` (C-31) is ε-universal for `σ`. No algebraic entries, no inverse-stability,
no spectral gap. -/
def UniversalitySphereDense (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : ℕ) (Φ : Fin p → SO (d + 1)),
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO (d + 1))) : Set (SO (d + 1))) →
    ∀ 𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow (RoundSphere (d + 1))), IsRichSphericalModel Φ 𝓕 →
      IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume (d + 1)) 𝓕

/-- **On `𝕊^d`, `d ≥ 1`, the density form holds.** -/
theorem universalitySphereDense_of_one_le {d : ℕ} (hd : 1 ≤ d) : UniversalitySphereDense d :=
  fun _ Φ hdense 𝓕 hrich => universality_sphere (by omega) Φ hdense 𝓕 hrich

/-- Every subgroup generated by a family of `SO(1) = {1}` is dense. -/
theorem dense_closure_SO_one {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → SO 1) :
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO 1)) : Set (SO 1)) := by
  have h : ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range Φ) : Subgroup (SO 1)) : Set (SO 1)) = univ :=
    Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun A => by rw [eq_one_of_SO_one A]; exact one_mem _
  rw [h]
  exact dense_univ

/-- **On `𝕊⁰` the density form fails**: `SO(1)` is trivial, so the identity generates a dense
subgroup, yet the `L²` model at it is not ε-universal on the two points of `S⁰`. The hypothesis
`2 ≤ n` of `universality_sphere` cannot be dropped. -/
theorem not_universalitySphereDense_zero : ¬ UniversalitySphereDense 0 := fun h =>
  (not_universality_sphere_identity one_pos).2
    (h 1 ![(1 : SO 1)] (dense_closure_SO_one _) _ (isRichSphericalModel_l2 one_pos _))

/-- **The density form of Theorem 3.6 holds exactly on the spheres of positive dimension.** -/
theorem universalitySphereDense_iff (d : ℕ) : UniversalitySphereDense d ↔ 1 ≤ d := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, universalitySphereDense_of_one_le⟩
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos d with h0 | h0
  · subst h0
    exact absurd h not_universalitySphereDense_zero
  · exact h0

/-- **Non-vacuity on `𝕊¹`**: the rotation of cosine `3/5` and its inverse (`so2Witness`). -/
theorem universality_sphere_witness_two :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume 2) (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel two_pos so2Witness)) :=
  universality_sphere_l2 le_rfl two_pos so2Witness so2Witness_dense

/-! ## `𝕊²`: a dense algebraic family of four rotations of `SO(3)`, Euler angles -/

theorem rotZ_mem (t : ℝ) :
    !![Real.cos t, -Real.sin t, 0; Real.sin t, Real.cos t, 0; 0, 0, 1] ∈
      Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin 3) ℝ := by
  rw [Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_orthogonalGroup_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · ext i j
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
      simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three] <;> nlinarith [Real.cos_sq_add_sin_sq t]
  · rw [Matrix.det_fin_three]
    simp
    nlinarith [Real.cos_sq_add_sin_sq t]

theorem rotX_mem (t : ℝ) :
    !![1, 0, 0; 0, Real.cos t, -Real.sin t; 0, Real.sin t, Real.cos t] ∈
      Matrix.specialOrthogonalGroup (Fin 3) ℝ := by
  rw [Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_iff, Matrix.mem_orthogonalGroup_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · ext i j
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
      simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three] <;> nlinarith [Real.cos_sq_add_sin_sq t]
  · rw [Matrix.det_fin_three]
    simp
    nlinarith [Real.cos_sq_add_sin_sq t]

/-- **The rotation of angle `t` about the third axis** of `ℝ³`. -/
noncomputable def rotZ (t : ℝ) : SO 3 := ⟨_, rotZ_mem t⟩

/-- **The rotation of angle `t` about the first axis** of `ℝ³`. -/
noncomputable def rotX (t : ℝ) : SO 3 := ⟨_, rotX_mem t⟩

theorem coe_rotZ (t : ℝ) : (rotZ t : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) =
    !![Real.cos t, -Real.sin t, 0; Real.sin t, Real.cos t, 0; 0, 0, 1] := rfl

theorem coe_rotX (t : ℝ) : (rotX t : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) =
    !![1, 0, 0; 0, Real.cos t, -Real.sin t; 0, Real.sin t, Real.cos t] := rfl

theorem rotZ_add (s t : ℝ) : rotZ (s + t) = rotZ s * rotZ t := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotZ (s + t) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) =
    (rotZ s : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) * (rotZ t : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ)
  rw [coe_rotZ, coe_rotZ, coe_rotZ, Matrix.mul_fin_three, Real.cos_add, Real.sin_add]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> ring

theorem rotX_add (s t : ℝ) : rotX (s + t) = rotX s * rotX t := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotX (s + t) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) =
    (rotX s : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) * (rotX t : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ)
  rw [coe_rotX, coe_rotX, coe_rotX, Matrix.mul_fin_three, Real.cos_add, Real.sin_add]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> ring

theorem rotZ_zero : rotZ 0 = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotZ 0 : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) = 1
  rw [coe_rotZ, Matrix.one_fin_three]
  simp

theorem rotX_zero : rotX 0 = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotX 0 : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) = 1
  rw [coe_rotX, Matrix.one_fin_three]
  simp

theorem rotZ_two_pi : rotZ (2 * Real.pi) = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotZ (2 * Real.pi) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) = 1
  rw [coe_rotZ, Matrix.one_fin_three]
  simp

theorem rotX_two_pi : rotX (2 * Real.pi) = 1 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  show (rotX (2 * Real.pi) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) = 1
  rw [coe_rotX, Matrix.one_fin_three]
  simp

/-- `t ↦ rotZ t` as a homomorphism `ℝ → SO(3)`. -/
noncomputable def rotZHom : Multiplicative ℝ →* SO 3 where
  toFun t := rotZ t.toAdd
  map_one' := rotZ_zero
  map_mul' s t := rotZ_add s.toAdd t.toAdd

/-- `t ↦ rotX t` as a homomorphism `ℝ → SO(3)`. -/
noncomputable def rotXHom : Multiplicative ℝ →* SO 3 where
  toFun t := rotX t.toAdd
  map_one' := rotX_zero
  map_mul' s t := rotX_add s.toAdd t.toAdd

theorem rotZ_neg (t : ℝ) : rotZ (-t) = (rotZ t)⁻¹ :=
  map_inv rotZHom (Multiplicative.ofAdd t)

theorem rotX_neg (t : ℝ) : rotX (-t) = (rotX t)⁻¹ :=
  map_inv rotXHom (Multiplicative.ofAdd t)

theorem continuous_rotZ : Continuous rotZ := by
  refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
  show Continuous fun t : ℝ => (!![Real.cos t, -Real.sin t, 0; Real.sin t, Real.cos t, 0; 0, 0, 1] :
    Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ)
  refine continuous_pi fun i => continuous_pi fun j => ?_
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> fun_prop

theorem continuous_rotX : Continuous rotX := by
  refine continuous_induced_rng.2 ?_
  show Continuous fun t : ℝ => (!![1, 0, 0; 0, Real.cos t, -Real.sin t; 0, Real.sin t, Real.cos t] :
    Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ)
  refine continuous_pi fun i => continuous_pi fun j => ?_
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp <;> fun_prop

/-- Every point of the unit circle has an angle. -/
theorem exists_angle {c s : ℝ} (h : c ^ 2 + s ^ 2 = 1) :
    ∃ t, Real.cos t = c ∧ Real.sin t = s := by
  set z : ℂ := ⟨c, s⟩
  have hz : ‖z‖ = 1 := by
    rw [Complex.norm_def, Complex.normSq_mk, show c * c + s * s = 1 by nlinarith, Real.sqrt_one]
  have hz0 : z ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0; rw [h0, norm_zero] at hz; exact zero_ne_one hz
  exact ⟨Complex.arg z, by rw [Complex.cos_arg hz0, hz, div_one],
    by rw [Complex.sin_arg, hz, div_one]⟩

theorem SO.mul_transpose {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) :
    (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) * (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)ᵀ = 1 :=
  (Matrix.mem_orthogonalGroup_iff (Fin n) ℝ).1 (Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_iff.1 A.2).1

theorem SO.transpose_mul {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) :
    (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)ᵀ * (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) = 1 :=
  (Matrix.mem_orthogonalGroup_iff' (Fin n) ℝ).1 (Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_iff.1 A.2).1

theorem SO.det_eq_one {n : ℕ} (A : SO n) : (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ).det = 1 :=
  (Matrix.mem_specialOrthogonalGroup_iff.1 A.2).2

/-- **The stabilizer of `e₃` in `SO(3)` is the group of rotations about the third axis.** -/
theorem exists_rotZ_of_fix (B : SO 3) (h0 : (B : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) 0 2 = 0)
    (h1 : (B : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) 1 2 = 0) (h2 : (B : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) 2 2 = 1) :
    ∃ c, rotZ c = B := by
  have hBB := SO.mul_transpose B
  have hdet := SO.det_eq_one B
  have e00 := congrFun (congrFun hBB 0) 0
  have e11 := congrFun (congrFun hBB 1) 1
  have e22 := congrFun (congrFun hBB 2) 2
  simp only [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three, Matrix.transpose_apply, Matrix.one_apply_eq,
    h0, h1, h2] at e00 e11 e22
  rw [Matrix.det_fin_three, h0, h1, h2] at hdet
  set M := (B : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ)
  have h20 : M 2 0 = 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (M 2 0), sq_nonneg (M 2 1)]
  have h21 : M 2 1 = 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (M 2 0), sq_nonneg (M 2 1)]
  have hsq : (M 1 1 - M 0 0) ^ 2 + (M 1 0 + M 0 1) ^ 2 = 0 := by
    linear_combination e11 + e00 - 2 * hdet
  have h11 : M 1 1 = M 0 0 := by
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (M 1 1 - M 0 0), sq_nonneg (M 1 0 + M 0 1)]
  have h10 : M 1 0 = -M 0 1 := by
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (M 1 1 - M 0 0), sq_nonneg (M 1 0 + M 0 1)]
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hs⟩ := exists_angle (c := M 0 0) (s := M 1 0) (by rw [h10]; nlinarith)
  refine ⟨c, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  show (rotZ c : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) = M
  rw [coe_rotZ, hc, hs]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [h0, h1, h2, h20, h21, h11, h10]

/-- **Euler angles**: every `A ∈ SO(3)` is `R_z(a) R_x(b) R_z(c)`. -/
theorem so3_euler (A : SO 3) : ∃ a b c : ℝ, rotZ a * rotX b * rotZ c = A := by
  have hAA := SO.transpose_mul A
  have e22 := congrFun (congrFun hAA 2) 2
  simp only [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three, Matrix.transpose_apply,
    Matrix.one_apply_eq] at e22
  set N := (A : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) with hN
  set b := Real.arccos (N 2 2)
  have hcb : Real.cos b = N 2 2 :=
    Real.cos_arccos (by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (N 0 2), sq_nonneg (N 1 2), sq_nonneg (N 2 2 + 1)])
      (by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (N 0 2), sq_nonneg (N 1 2), sq_nonneg (N 2 2 - 1)])
  have hsb2 : Real.sin b ^ 2 = N 0 2 ^ 2 + N 1 2 ^ 2 := by
    have := Real.sin_sq_add_cos_sq b
    rw [hcb] at this
    linarith
  obtain ⟨a, ha1, ha2⟩ : ∃ a, Real.sin a * Real.sin b = N 0 2 ∧
      -(Real.cos a * Real.sin b) = N 1 2 := by
    by_cases hs0 : Real.sin b = 0
    · rw [hs0] at hsb2
      refine ⟨0, ?_, ?_⟩
      · rw [hs0, mul_zero]; nlinarith [sq_nonneg (N 0 2), sq_nonneg (N 1 2)]
      · rw [hs0, mul_zero, neg_zero]; nlinarith [sq_nonneg (N 0 2), sq_nonneg (N 1 2)]
    · obtain ⟨a, hc, hs⟩ := exists_angle (c := -N 1 2 / Real.sin b) (s := N 0 2 / Real.sin b)
        (by rw [div_pow, div_pow, neg_sq, ← add_div, add_comm, ← hsb2]
            exact div_self (pow_ne_zero 2 hs0))
      refine ⟨a, ?_, ?_⟩
      · rw [hs]; field_simp
      · rw [hc]; field_simp
  set M := rotZ a * rotX b with hM
  have hcol : ∀ i, (M : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i 2 = N i 2 := by
    intro i
    show ((rotZ a : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) * (rotX b : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ)) i 2 = N i 2
    rw [coe_rotZ, coe_rotX]
    fin_cases i <;> simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three] <;> linarith
  set B := M⁻¹ * A with hB
  have hBcol : ∀ i, (B : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i 2 = (1 : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i 2 := by
    intro i
    have h1 : ((M⁻¹ * M : SO 3) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) = 1 := by rw [inv_mul_cancel]; rfl
    calc (B : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i 2
        = ∑ k, ((M⁻¹ : SO 3) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i k * N k 2 := Matrix.mul_apply
      _ = ∑ k, ((M⁻¹ : SO 3) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i k *
            (M : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) k 2 := by simp_rw [hcol]
      _ = ((M⁻¹ * M : SO 3) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i 2 := Matrix.mul_apply.symm
      _ = (1 : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) i 2 := by rw [h1]
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_rotZ_of_fix B (by simpa using hBcol 0) (by simpa using hBcol 1)
    (by simpa using hBcol 2)
  refine ⟨a, b, c, ?_⟩
  rw [hc, hB, ← hM, mul_inv_cancel_left]

/-- **The witness on `𝕊²`**: the rotations of cosine `3/5` about the third and the first axes,
and their inverses (two generators and their inverses, `p = 4`, as `main.tex:308`). -/
noncomputable def so3Witness : Fin 4 → SO 3 :=
  ![rotZ angle35, rotZ (-angle35), rotX angle35, rotX (-angle35)]

/-- **The witness generates a dense subgroup of `SO(3)`**: the closure of the generated group
contains both one-parameter subgroups (`θ/(2π)` irrational, Niven), hence every product given by
the Euler angles (`so3_euler`). -/
theorem so3Witness_dense :
    Dense ((Subgroup.closure (Set.range so3Witness) : Subgroup (SO 3)) : Set (SO 3)) := by
  set Γ := Subgroup.closure (Set.range so3Witness)
  have hZ : ∀ t, rotZ t ∈ Γ.topologicalClosure := fun t =>
    Subgroup.topologicalClosure_mono (Subgroup.zpowers_le.2
      (Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_range_self (0 : Fin 4))))
      (mem_topologicalClosure_zpowers rotZHom continuous_rotZ rotZ_two_pi irrational_angle35 t)
  have hX : ∀ t, rotX t ∈ Γ.topologicalClosure := fun t =>
    Subgroup.topologicalClosure_mono (Subgroup.zpowers_le.2
      (Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_range_self (2 : Fin 4))))
      (mem_topologicalClosure_zpowers rotXHom continuous_rotX rotX_two_pi irrational_angle35 t)
  intro A
  obtain ⟨a, b, c, rfl⟩ := so3_euler A
  rw [← Subgroup.topologicalClosure_coe]
  exact Γ.topologicalClosure.mul_mem (Γ.topologicalClosure.mul_mem (hZ a) (hX b)) (hZ c)

theorem so3Witness_inv (i : Fin 4) : ∃ j, so3Witness j = (so3Witness i)⁻¹ := by
  fin_cases i
  · exact ⟨1, by simp [so3Witness, rotZ_neg]⟩
  · exact ⟨0, by simp [so3Witness, rotZ_neg]⟩
  · exact ⟨3, by simp [so3Witness, rotX_neg]⟩
  · exact ⟨2, by simp [so3Witness, rotX_neg]⟩

/-- **The witness has algebraic (indeed rational) entries**: `0, 1, 3/5, ±4/5`. -/
theorem so3Witness_algebraic (i : Fin 4) (a b : Fin 3) :
    IsAlgebraic ℤ ((so3Witness i : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ) a b) := by
  have hc : IsAlgebraic ℤ (Real.cos angle35) := by
    rw [cos_angle35, show (3 / 5 : ℝ) = ((3 / 5 : ℚ) : ℝ) by push_cast; ring]
    exact isAlgebraic_ratCast _
  have hs : IsAlgebraic ℤ (Real.sin angle35) := by
    rw [sin_angle35, show (4 / 5 : ℝ) = ((4 / 5 : ℚ) : ℝ) by push_cast; ring]
    exact isAlgebraic_ratCast _
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases a <;> fin_cases b <;>
    simp [so3Witness, coe_rotZ, coe_rotX, Real.cos_neg, Real.sin_neg] <;>
    first
    | exact hc | exact hs | exact hs.neg | exact isAlgebraic_zero | exact isAlgebraic_one

/-- **Non-vacuity on `𝕊²`**, the sphere of the experiments (`main.tex:496`): the `L²` model at
`so3Witness` is ε-universal. -/
theorem universality_sphere_witness_three :
    IsUniversalFamilyEps (sphereVolume 3)
      (isometrySphericalFamily (l2SphericalModel (by norm_num) so3Witness)) :=
  universality_sphere_l2 (by norm_num) (by norm_num) so3Witness so3Witness_dense

/-- **On `𝕊²` the printed Theorem 3.6 is false** (C-31): `so3Witness` meets the technical
assumption of `main.tex:836` (stable under inverse, dense, algebraic entries), and the constant
model at it is not ε-universal. -/
theorem not_universalitySpherePrinted_two : ¬ UniversalitySpherePrinted 2 :=
  not_universalitySpherePrinted (d := 2) (by norm_num) so3Witness
    ⟨so3Witness_inv, so3Witness_dense, so3Witness_algebraic⟩

end EGF
